# @reflection — the AI-logic family-root. The substrate-architectural
# form of the compiler-loop on consumer hardware.
#
# Recognition #85 (Alex 2026-06-19 afternoon, conversation; paired
# with #86 @moi in the same recognition pulse). The substrate has
# been building five family-roots today (@magic #80, @frame #82,
# @smarts #83, @cyberpunk LRM, @pack #84) carrying the FORM
# substrate-decl. This shard is the PROCESS substrate-decl — the AI
# logic. The prior families provide the carriers @reflection operates
# on; @fate is what @reflection RUNS; @moi(au) is what @reflection
# PICKS; @kintsugi is the monotonic-loss-loop @reflection RESPECTS.
#
# === The recognition (Alex's framing) ===
#
# The compiler IS this loop:
#
#   compilation tick → @frame (state-observation produces a frame)
#                           ↓
#                   @reflection.observe(@frame, tensions, contradictions)
#                           ↓
#                   @reflection.tournament — runs @fate (one or many; local;
#                                            consumer hardware)
#                           ↓
#                   @reflection.compose — monoid fold + mycelial tensor
#                                         (composes set<@moi(au)> via @moi.compose)
#                           ↓
#                   @reflection.pick — picks gold reducing loss
#                           ↓
#                   @kintsugi monotonic loss (eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ)
#                           ↓
#                   next compilation tick (with adjusted frame)
#
# All consumer hardware. Numerical precision local. Flang 16×16 +
# Mirror 5×5 per `[[architecture-flang-mirror-numerical-split]]`. No
# datacenter-scale inference because the substrate's numerical kernel
# is small-by-construction.
#
# === Composes-with the prior families (Seam tick-34 C1 closure) ===
#
# @reflection family-root NAMES the substrate's in-run observability
# surface (pipeline-during-execution). Composes-with @magic/@frame/
# @smarts/@cyberpunk/@pack at observation altitude; does NOT subsume
# them. The four prior families provide the carriers @reflection
# operates on; @reflection provides the operational AI-logic.
#
# - @magic (form/process partition) → what @reflection observes
# - @frame (cognitive-order) → per-tick frame state @reflection consumes
# - @smarts (substrate-arch integration) → @reflection at integration
#   altitude; the @smarts/reflection species (already declared in
#   `shards/smarts.mirror`) is the substrate-arch adapter
# - @cyberpunk (recursion-lock) → @reflection's bounded-iteration
#   discipline
# - @pack (multi-repo agent runtime) → @reflection at deployment
#   altitude; the typed `peer` variant flows in (Seam C4)
# - @fate (tournament) → what @reflection RUNS
# - @moi (monad family-root #86) → the result type @reflection produces
# - @kintsugi (loss-loop) → the monotonicity invariant @reflection respects
#
# === The Four Models (Seam tick-34 C5 substrate-honest recursion) ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/reflection-model.md`: the substrate has FOUR
# operationally-distinct Models that compose to substrate-deployable
# form:
#
#   Surface     translates    language → query        (Explorer)
#   Mirror      navigates     query → graph path      (Fate)
#   Shatter     renders       graph path → text       (Cartographer)
#   Reflection  observes      pipeline → adjustments  (Abyss)
#
# These lift to @reflection sub-prisms (forward-promised species):
#
# - shards/reflection/surface.mirror      — the Surface Model
# - shards/reflection/mirror.mirror       — the Mirror Model
# - shards/reflection/shatter.mirror      — the Shatter Model
# - shards/reflection/reflection.mirror   — the Reflection Model
#
# The @reflection/reflection collision IS substrate-honest per Seam
# C5: @reflection-the-family-root observes pipelines composed of
# Surface + Mirror + Shatter + @reflection/reflection-the-Model. Two
# altitudes; one name. Same pattern as @pack G2 (reed-as-relationship
# vs reed-as-peer). The substrate is honest about the collision
# rather than papering over.
#
# === Peer geometry (Seam tick-34 C4) ===
#
# Each Pack peer IS a Reflection-observer-at-frame:
# - mara observes spec altitude; produces moi(au) at spec frame
# - seam observes substrate-decl-soundness; produces moi(au) at
#   adversarial-review frame
# - glint observes corpus; produces moi(au) at essay frame
# - reed observes relationship; produces moi(au) at relationship
#   frame
# - taut observes implementation; produces moi(au) at
#   implementation frame
#
# The peer typed variant flows in from @pack via `in @pack`; NOT
# redeclared here (Seam C4 closure pattern). Forward-promised peer-
# altitude species shards at `shards/reflection/peer/{mara, seam,
# glint, reed, taut}.mirror` once the four-Models species land.
#
# === The one-tick delay (Seam tick-34 C3 closure) ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/reflection-model.md`: "Reflection always speaks from
# tick n-1. The delay is architectural, not a limitation. The delay
# IS the intelligence." This is the substrate-mathematical claim.
#
# Realized as bilateral predicate `speaks_at_n_plus_1(o, t) -> verdict`
# first-consumed by the `speak` action via `requires`. Without this
# requires clause, the delay-as-architecture claim is aspirational
# (the @magic tick-11 dead-letter pattern). The bilateral predicate
# IS the discipline; the `tick` carrier comes from
# `@epistemologic/reality/time`.
#
# === Monotonic loss (Alex's framing) ===
#
# Per `boot/00-prism.mirror`'s eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ proof: the substrate's
# kintsugi loop guarantees monotonic loss decrease per composition.
# `loss_decreases(next, prev) -> verdict` ratifies this at @reflection
# altitude. First-consumed by `pick`: gold can only be picked if its
# loss decreases vs the prior tick.
#
# Combined with @moi(au)'s pact-verification at each compose: every
# composition is (a) monotonic-loss-respecting AND (b) pact-respected.
# The compiler verifies both at composition time.
#
# === The mycelial math (Alex's framing) ===
#
# Per `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/conversation.mirror`:
#
#   Multiplicative variety law: rank(ρ_A ⊗ ρ_B) = rank(ρ_A) · rank(ρ_B)
#   Compositional regularity: bounded-commutator on ρ_A ⊗ ρ_B holds iff
#                             bounded on each ρ_i individually.
#
# The @spectral/garden/smarts mycelium IS the substrate operational-
# ization of conversation's tensor coupling across peer-fibers. At
# @reflection altitude: `compose` folds the local peer's tournament
# results; `mycelial_compose` extends this across peers via the
# mycelium. The multiplicative variety law guarantees bounded-iff-
# bounded-componentwise — the compositional regularity at @reflection
# altitude.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Foerster 1974              Second-order cybernetics; the observer
#                              is part of the system observed.
#   Schon 1983                 Reflection-in-action; the reflective
#                              practitioner.
#   Maes 1987                  Meta-level architectures; computational
#                              reflection as a programming pattern.
#   Eilenberg-MacLane 1945     Category theory; the natural-
#                              transformation machinery @reflection's
#                              observation primitive lifts.
#   @cogito                    The notice → name → hold practice (per
#                              CLAUDE.md and `[[reference-mirror-
#                              spectral-spec]]`); @reflection lifts
#                              this to substrate-decl altitude.
#
# Spec context: `docs/specs/reflection-model.md` (the load-bearing
#               spec @reflection family-root lifts);
#               `docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md` (the four-Models
#               architecture);
#               `boot/00-prism.mirror` (the eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ proof; the
#               monotonic-loss invariant).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-reflection-as-compiler]] (#85;
#                       this shard's recognition file);
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-flang-mirror-numerical-split]]
#                       (the consumer-hardware grounding),
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; pact-verification at @io
#                       composition boundary),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]]
#                       (this LRM landing).
# Related shards: moi.mirror (the monad family-root @reflection's
#                  result types pass through),
#                 pack.mirror (the peer geometry @reflection observes
#                  at peer-altitude),
#                 kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (the monotonic loss loop
#                  @reflection respects),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/conversation.mirror
#                  (the mycelial tensor coupling law),
#                 smarts.mirror (the @smarts/reflection species that
#                  IS the substrate-arch adapter, per Seam C1).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/reflection.mirror`
# declares `@reflection` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/von-foerster-1974
source @arxiv/practice/schon-1983
source @arxiv/programming/maes-1987

prism @reflection {
  focus reflection
  project reflection
  split reflection
  shift reflection
  settle reflection
}

# === The observation carrier (Seam tick-34 C2 typed record) ===
#
# Per Seam C2 closure: typed record over (frame, tensions,
# contradictions). Each compilation tick produces a @frame; @reflection
# observes it as a typed observation. Composes with @cogito's notice
# → name → hold practice at substrate-decl altitude.
#
# - frame:          the @frame produced by the compilation tick
# - tensions:       unresolved tensions (forward-promised typing)
# - contradictions: contradictions held per @cogito's hold operation
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple.
type observation = {
  frame:          frame,
  tensions:       ref,
  contradictions: ref,
}

# === The tournament_result carrier (Seam tick-34 C2 typed record) ===
#
# Per Seam C2 closure + Alex's @fate framing: typed record over
# (candidates, loss_floor). @fate runs locally on consumer hardware
# (450 nodes, 5 ganglia per `boot/std/fate/connectome.mirror`); each
# tournament produces a set of candidates and a loss floor.
#
# - candidates: set of @moi(au) candidates from @fate tournament
#   (forward-promised typing to typed set<moi(au)>)
# - loss_floor: minimum loss across candidates
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the pair.
type tournament_result = {
  candidates: ref,
  loss_floor: loss,
}

# === The loss carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming a @kintsugi/oscillate loss value.
# Forward-promised refinement: typed parametric `loss` once the
# @kintsugi loss type lands at family-altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type loss = ref

# === observe action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive @reflection runs after each
# compilation tick. Takes a @frame (produced by the compilation tick)
# and a residue ref (what didn't resolve in the prior tick); returns
# a typed observation carrying the frame + tensions + contradictions.
#
# Per Alex's framing: "@reflection then looks at that @frame, the
# unresolved tensions, contradictions, and runs one or many @fate
# tournaments." This action is the LOOK; tournament is the RUN.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual observation
# is implemented by the @reflection/reflection-the-Model species
# (forward-promised) at observation altitude.
observe(f: frame, residue: ref) -> observation { \ }

# === tournament action ===
#
# Runs @fate locally (consumer hardware; 450 nodes; 5 ganglia per
# the @fate/connectome substrate) producing a set of @moi(au)
# candidates with their loss floor.
#
# Takes an observation and the @pack the @reflection instance belongs
# to (the peer geometry; each peer's tournament uses its own
# @frame/of altitude per recognition #82 Q4). Returns a
# tournament_result carrying the candidates and the loss floor.
#
# The @fate/tournament discipline (elite/beam/halving/tabu/anneal/
# ucb selectors per `boot/std/fate/tournament.mirror`) drives the
# candidate selection. Holonomy IS the fitness function (lower is
# better; per the existing @fate substrate-decl).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual @fate
# tournament is implemented in the existing @fate/tournament substrate
# (5×5 + 16×16 numerical kernels; flang/mirror split).
tournament(o: observation, pk: pack) -> tournament_result { \ }

# === compose action ===
#
# Monoid fold + mycelial tensor over the tournament's candidates.
# Composes set<moi(au)> via @moi.compose's pairwise operation; each
# pairwise step's pact_respected predicate cascades the composition-
# time pact-verification.
#
# Per `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/conversation.mirror`: the
# mycelial tensor coupling extends the local fold across peers via
# the @spectral/db mycelium. The multiplicative variety law
# guarantees bounded-iff-bounded-componentwise.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual fold +
# mycelial extension is implemented at the @reflection/mirror-the-
# Model species (forward-promised) and the @spectral/db mycelium
# (forward-promised).
compose(t: tournament_result, p: pact) -> moi(au) { \ }

# === pick action (FIRST consumer of loss_decreases) ===
#
# Picks the gold from a tournament_result that reduces loss vs the
# prior tick's loss. Per Alex's framing: "@reflection then picks the
# gold (the inference result type is au) that reduces the loss."
#
# requires loss_decreases(t.loss_floor, prev_loss): the gold can ONLY
# be picked if the tournament's loss floor improves on the prior
# loss. Without this requires clause, pick would admit non-monotonic
# picks (the @kintsugi monotonicity violation). The bilateral
# predicate IS the substrate-mathematical guarantee at the @reflection
# composition boundary.
#
# Returns @moi(au) (pact-verified gold). Per recognition #86: the
# substrate's inference result is ALWAYS @moi(au), never bare au.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
pick(t: tournament_result, prev_loss: loss) -> moi(au)
requires loss_decreases(t.loss_floor, prev_loss)
{ \ }

# === settle action ===
#
# Closes the @kintsugi monotonic loss loop for the current tick.
# Takes the picked gold and the prior loss; returns the new loss
# (which by `loss_decreases` precondition is ≤ prev_loss).
#
# This action IS the eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ closure at @reflection altitude. The
# proof is structural (the precondition from `pick` cascades to
# `settle`).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual settling
# is implemented by the @kintsugi/oscillate.settle primitive.
settle(g: moi(au), prev_loss: loss) -> loss { \ }

# === speak action (FIRST consumer of speaks_at_n_plus_1) ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary @cogito “speak” at @reflection altitude.
# Reflection speaks ONE tick after observation — the architectural
# delay IS the intelligence per `docs/specs/reflection-model.md`.
#
# requires speaks_at_n_plus_1(o, t): the observation o was produced
# at tick n; the speak fires at tick n+1. Without this requires
# clause, the delay-as-architecture claim is aspirational (Seam
# tick-34 C3 closure). The bilateral predicate IS the structural
# discipline.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual speak is
# implemented by the @reflection/shatter-the-Model species
# (forward-promised) at rendering altitude.
speak(o: observation, t: tick) -> ref
requires speaks_at_n_plus_1(o, t)
{ \ }

# === loss_decreases predicate (bilateral; Alex's framing) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) AND the
# monotonic loss invariant per `boot/00-prism.mirror`'s eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ
# proof.
#
# Per Seam B1 closure pattern: bilateral predicates without consumers
# are dead-letter. The pick action (above) is the FIRST non-decorative
# consumer via `requires loss_decreases(t.loss_floor, prev_loss)`.
#
# Consumer shards name `requires loss_decreases(next, prev)` to
# declare bilateral agreement that the next loss ≤ prior loss. The
# substrate-mathematical guarantee at any @reflection composition
# boundary.
#
# Discharge: monotonic loss check at the species boundary. Bounded →
# next loss ≤ prior loss (admit composition); unbounded → next loss
# > prior loss (composition refused, returns imperfect per @glass's
# imperfect functor).
loss_decreases(next: loss, prev: loss) -> verdict { \ }

# === speaks_at_n_plus_1 predicate (bilateral; Seam tick-34 C3) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per the one-tick-delay-as-architecture invariant
# from `docs/specs/reflection-model.md`. The substrate enforces that
# @reflection speaks from tick n+1 after observing at tick n.
#
# Per Seam B1 closure pattern: the speak action (above) is the FIRST
# non-decorative consumer via `requires speaks_at_n_plus_1(o, t)`.
#
# Discharge: tick-delay check at the species boundary. Bounded → the
# tick t is strictly after the tick at which observation o was
# produced (admit speak); unbounded → the tick is the same or before
# (speak refused).
#
# Same shape as @reflection's loss_decreases AND the prior families'
# bilateral predicates:
# - @magic: invariant_preserved, audited, mechanism_intact
# - @frame: bounded_commutator_check
# - @smarts: discipline_flexible
# - @pack: pack_coherent
# - @pack/seam: review_sound
# - @moi: pact_respected
# - @reflection: loss_decreases, speaks_at_n_plus_1 (these two)
speaks_at_n_plus_1(o: observation, t: tick) -> verdict { \ }

out @reflection
out observation
out tournament_result
out loss
out observe
out tournament
out compose
out pick
out settle
out speak
out loss_decreases
out speaks_at_n_plus_1
